  {
    "id": "how",
    "title": "Delegate, never surrender",
    "labels": [
      "Revocable mandate",
      "Effective exit",
      "Remedy"
    ],
    "lines": [
      "Administration may be delegated to automated systems, but collective goals must stay under legitimate control.",
      "A right to leave a provider counts only if identity, records and services move too.",
      "An appeal needs reasons, corrected facts, independent review and a real remedy.",
      "Those who set goals, run infrastructure and oversee rights must remain separate powers."
    ],
    "emotionalPlan": {
      "arc": "Steady construction of safeguards, each one adding firmness.",
      "purpose": "Show the book's method: concrete institutional conditions that keep delegation revocable.",
      "states": [
        "deliberate",
        "practical",
        "exacting",
        "assured"
      ],
      "intensities": [
        0.5,
        0.5,
        0.6,
        0.6
      ],
      "voiceDirections": [
        "Measured; contrast delegated with must stay.",
        "Practical, with a slight emphasis on move too.",
        "Crisp, giving each requirement its own beat.",
        "Confident and even, closing the argument."
      ]
    },
    "chapter": "02 · Delegate, never surrender",
